WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.400
The swaying of Fa and Kamille's hearts
led to Fa's actions to dash out on her own.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:44.200
Meanwhile, Scirocco only watched
as Jerid also dashed out on his own.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.610
In these incidents, each individual was
trying to find their own path.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.620
Moon Attack

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.810
May I also go to the Argama,
Lieutenant Quattro?!

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.490
- Are you happy?
- Of course!

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.160
The Argama's similar to the White Base,
right?

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.890
The White Base was full of life.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:39.370
Mr. Wong, our operation has begun!

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.340
I never whimsically plan to
fight a war.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.270
I'll talk to him.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.830
- Lieutenant Quattro told you, did he?
- Yes!

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.850
Okay, standby on the mobile suit deck!

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.010
Yes, sir!

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:58.320
<i>Lieutenant Quattro, you'll also have to</i>
<i>work as bodyguard for Commodore Blex.</i>

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:03.220
However, yesterday you gave us
permission to launch today.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.120
<i>The situation has changed!</i>

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.130
<i>It's not wise for us to make</i>
<i>any careless moves...</i>

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.160
<i>...before the Earth Federation</i>
<i>Government General Assembly!</i>

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:14.300
It's been confirmed that the Titans' fleet
is headed for Von Braun City.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.730
<i>We're not under attack yet.</i>

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.470
It would be too late once attacked!

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:23.400
The outcome of war is decided by
your planning before and after battle.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.470
Let's trust that our
decisions are correct.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.840
<i>All right.</i>

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.180
It would help if the Titans intercepted
this wireless communication.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.250
They'd assume the A.E.U.G.
is split internally.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.230
I've never heard of a bodyguard
for Commodore Blex.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.420
Is that also a lie?

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.320
I'll go if time permits.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.430
Wait a minute.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.990
The Commodore's telling us to observe
the face of our true enemy.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.000
- When?
- During this operation.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:03:59.980
Kamille!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.010
Miss Emma?

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.380
What are you doing?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:03.970
I'm cleaning my room.

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:06.280
But we're on our way
to the Operation Zone!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.820
You should be doing this
while in spaceport!

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.260
I could die, you know!

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.360
I'd better leave this place clean,
or the birds will laugh at me!

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.030
If you put things in the hallway...

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.930
...you're blocking passage
in the case of an emergency!

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.760
The auto-cleaner doesn't do the job.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.230
It doesn't clean the little corners.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.960
What'll you do if we enter
a battle situation?

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.600
You haven't prepped
the Zeta Gundam yet, have you?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.300
I'm just about finished!

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:29.700
- I'll help.
- I can carry it, Miss Emma.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.120
If I let you do this alone,
who knows how long it'll take you!

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:42.450
You're still being easy on yourself,
as a victim who lost his parents, right?

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.820
No way!

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:47.550
Now, I think more about the pilots
who I've ended up killing.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.260
- Do you pray for them?
- Although I have no religion.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.660
Religion is irrelevant to those
who have passed away, isn't it?

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.970
When is this war going to end?

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.700
Ask Lieutenant Quattro.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.000
Is the Lieutenant coming?

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.010
Sorry!

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.480
You're going up to the bridge, right?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:06.670
Kamille.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.270
There's something I want to give Torres.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.180
I'll give it to him for you.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.680
- B-But.
- What's the matter?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.060
What I said earlier, I was talking
about the way you deal with others.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:18.960
Bye.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:19.990
Hey.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.150
What is it, Fa?!

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.200
May I have a word, Lieutenant?!

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.790
There are some parts of the manual
that I don't understand.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.700
Okay, sure. I'll be right back.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.740
Mr. Astonaige was very upset.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.780
Really?

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:47.710
Von Braun City is built around
Captain Armstrong's footprint, right?

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.650
Yeah, it's where humanity landed
for the first time.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:50.850
Here you are.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.830
Lieutenant Emma, what is it?

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.520
It's from Kamille.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.990
He asked me to give it to you.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.260
From Kamille?!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.160
Th-Thank you.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.200
- Did you want me?
- Thanks for coming.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.330
What is it?

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:07.140
- A gift from Hong Kong!
- Show me later.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:09.270
I hope you're searching for enemies!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.310
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.270
We're receiving goods from the Radish.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.580
Y-Yes!

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.080
We'll also be asking pilots to help out.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:16.620
Yes, sir!

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.760
Mouar will lead our second battle unit.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.860
Jerid's unit will be our first unit...

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.900
...with Chief Petty Officer Holly
replacing Chief Petty Officer Siddeley.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.440
What is Operation Apollo, Sarah Zabiarov?

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:41.440
Yes...

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:45.610
...Von Braun City is believed to be
the ideal focal point to build a base...

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.480
...since from there both Earth and the
far side of the Moon can be conquered.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.350
- Therefore, by controlling the location...!
- Very good, Chief Petty Officer.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.020
You seem to possess some good qualities.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.950
However, I have allowed Chief Petty
Officer Siddeley to die out there.

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.360
Do you really believe so?

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:01.730
Jerid.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:06.300
Siddeley was killed in action...solely
because she lacked the strengths required.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.460
Isn't that right, Lieutenant Jerid?

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:14.900
Chief Petty Officer Siddeley
carried out her duties excellently.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:15.940
Jerid!

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:16.940
Never mind him!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.100
Our strategic meeting is over.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:23.510
He went ahead to the mobile suits deck
because he understands his responsibilities.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.350
You'd better all hurry, too!

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:31.960
Lieutenant Commander Jamaican...

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.420
- ...are you okay with this?
- Sure.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:38.360
He'll be the one acting as a shield
to the Alexandria.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.900
That's just one way we can use him.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:41.940
I see.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.600
So we can look at it that way, can we?

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.160
Must I spell it out for you?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:51.600
How are things on your end?!

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.200
Okay. Please connect the cord!

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.180
Are you done equipping the Methuss?

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:09.220
I thought they were joking earlier,
but Miss Emma's actually teaching Fa.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.760
How are you doing, Kamille?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:11.800
Miss Emma?!

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.970
- Then who's that?
- It's Ensign Reccoa and Fa.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.670
<i>Come to think of it, it's abnormal</i>
<i>for so many women...</i>

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.900
<i>...to come out front in the battlefield</i>
<i>that belongs to men.</i>

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.670
<i>This world is changing.</i>

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:34.550
We should be joining the Radish
any time now.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:44.930
What do you mean?
Is a war going to break out?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.360
Can this launch take off?

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.600
Okay, we're leaving for the Argama.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.270
- Will we begin fighting?
- That's why we're in such a hurry!

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:01.840
<i>Can you hear me, Lieutenant Quattro?!</i>

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.680
<i>We've located the enemy fleet.</i>

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.220
<i>We'll have to postpone delivery of goods.</i>

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.380
Roger!

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.980
What's the status of the reinforcements
from Granada?

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.220
We have no response!

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.890
The Titans were not misled
by our false communication.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.190
They're still headed for Von Braun City.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.230
<i>Captain!</i>

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.500
I want to directly make contact
with the enemy ships!

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.160
<i>Roger, I'll send reinforcements right away.</i>

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.900
Make sure you come back!

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.570
<i>I'll have to if I want to work</i>
<i>with the Commodore.</i>

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:27.740
Exactly!

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:29.670
Hyaku Shiki, taking off!

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:30.870
<i>Go ahead!</i>

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.880
The mobile suit unit has left!

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.990
All units in battle positions!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.790
Okay, commencing Operation Apollo!

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.820
All vessels are to fire warning shots
at Von Braun City!

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.690
Following that, send out mobile suits!

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.800
After that, the Dogosse Gier
will command the battle.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:53.800
So follow their orders.

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:55.730
Send the message to all vessels!

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.740
All battle commands after this
to come from the Dogosse Gier!

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:01.260
Now, let's observe how
Scirocco handles this.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:04.240
Leave the central district
of Von Braun City intact!

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:06.250
It's the city we will be using as our base!

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:07.650
Fire warning shots to surrounding areas!

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.040
What's that?!

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.420
They're using long-range missiles
and beams for warning shots!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.560
Caesar! All units to take
level one battle stations!

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.230
We'll drag this into a mobile suits battle!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.740
The Radish's launch has arrived!

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.170
Worry about that later!
Let them handle that by themselves!

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.880
Standby here until we receive
further orders.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:41.010
Mobile suits will be taking off!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.140
Where are you going?!

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:42.840
Roger!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.780
Okay! More to the front!

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:47.680
- <i>I'm</i> getting on!
- But...!

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:49.380
Kamille!

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.360
- Haro!
- Kamille! Kamille!

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:53.180
Kamille!

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.190
- The two of you!
- Kamille! She...!

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:57.500
Fa!

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.430
Who are you?!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.060
You're in our way!
Get back to where you belong!

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.070
I've come to fight as well!

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:02.860
Katz!

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.230
I don't want to see what happened
in San Francisco again!

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.470
<i>Kamille! Hurry!</i>

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:07.200
Right!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.300
Katz!

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:11.340
Fa!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.870
Miss Reccoa.
If there's anything that I can do...!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.780
Katz, there aren't any spare mobile suits
here, you know. Not even one.

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:23.380
Gundam Mk. II, taking off!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:24.790
Roger!

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.020
- Apolly's Rick Dias unit has left!
- What about the Zeta Gundam?!

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.360
Taking off right now!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.560
Zeta Gundam! Taking off!

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:42.010
Don't send out the mobile suit unit yet!

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:44.400
Our objective is to take over
Von Braun City!

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.180
Why doesn't he send us out yet?

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.710
<i>Does Scirocco plan to take credit</i>
<i>for the best part of the attack?</i>

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.810
<i>That girl might know.</i>

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.780
Ignore all mobile suits that are not
closing in on Von Braun City.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:18.810
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.810
Move! If you remain still...!

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.260
It's because you're acting scared.

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:38.000
No mobile suits from the likely flagship,
but they're coming from the sides!

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:38.900
Above?!

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:43.500
Rick Dias unit countering!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:44.660
Follow me!

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.900
Fleet vessels, form a horizontal line!

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:51.140
Got to move quicker
to battle their mobile suits!

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:00.910
How could they fire anti-air battery...

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:02.460
...after sending out their own mobile suits?!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.370
What am I doing?!
I can do better!

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:37.160
I'm sinking that ship!

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.320
Enemy mobile suit heading this way, sir!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.920
If you have the time to talk,
fire back instead!

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:56.400
I can do this!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:03.720
Fa!

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:10.580
That's it!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:19.890
Are you all right?!

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:21.730
I would've been okay
by myself!

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:22.960
This is a battlefield!

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.160
Battle-field?

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.670
If we sink the Alexandria...!

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.270
<i>Apolly, behind you!</i>

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.550
We've entered Von Braun City territory!

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.420
Send out the Dogosse Gier
mobile suit unit!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.330
Scirocco!

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:47.720
So, you're leaving the A.E.U.G. for
Jamaican to handle...

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.760
...and grabbing all the goodies for yourself!

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:57.700
<i>Chief Petty Officers Sarah, Holly,</i>
<i>we'll descend at once to Von Braun City!</i>

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:58.600
Yes, Lieutenant!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.940
What?! A mobile suit team?!

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:07.340
They're acting independently of their
fleet; trying to enter Von Braun City!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.280
Times have changed! Oldtypes
should remain in the background!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:21.320
What?!

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:29.630
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.470
Lieutenant!

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:38.540
Chief Petty Officer Holly,
there are only two of them!

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:41.170
The enemy's holding back Jerid's team.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.220
The enemy consists of two?

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:44.270
That's right, sir.
Shall we send out Mouar's unit?

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.920
<i>We'll head there directly with this ship.</i>

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:49.790
<i>That should suffice as backup</i>
<i>for Jerid's unit.</i>

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.890
By "directly", does he mean
descend into Von Braun City?

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.060
If we're in Von Braun City,
the A.E.U.G. cannot attack us!

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:58.460
R-Roger.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:02.800
It certainly helps that Jerid
is keeping those two units occupied.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.900
He's doing a great job.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.670
He was using Jerid as a decoy.

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:09.130
Scirocco!

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:11.170
Open the airlock!

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:14.610
Mouar is attempting to sortie
at her own discretion.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:15.840
- Let her go.
- Huh?

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.240
Let her do as she wishes.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.020
What's the status on reinforcements
from Granada?

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:24.460
We've had no word from them since.

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.360
The longer it takes them,
the greater our disadvantage.

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.290
It's fine while the enemy's wavering...

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.330
...and forgetting about attacking
Von Braun City, but...!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:33.890
- Something's strange, Captain.
- What is it?

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.270
Just one vessel from the Titans' fleet
is descending!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.960
Don't let the Dogosse Gier
descend into Von Braun City alone!

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:44.180
- It's too late.
- After them at once!

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.650
What's on your mind, Scirocco?

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:49.110
Two dogs fight for a bone,
and a third runs away with it.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.150
I guess it was part of their plan...

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.190
...for the rear vessels
to look like they were wavering.

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:56.920
It's behind me!

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.020
Gotcha!

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.020
This unpleasantness...!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.730
Wh-What's this?

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:09.170
What is this unpleasantness?

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:12.600
This feeling...!
Could it be that man?

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.320
Wait, I'll finish him off!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.600
I won't allow that!

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:50.670
Jerid!

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:55.940
Kamille!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.920
Fall!

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:08.960
Mouar!

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:14.930
Jerid!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.570
Why did you get in my way, Mouar?

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:21.130
If you hadn't interfered...

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:22.680
<i>...I would've defeated Kamille!</i>

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:25.040
<i>But you would've been shot as well!</i>

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:31.010
You're being used as a decoy.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:33.050
You saw Scirocco descend
in the Dogosse Gier, didn't you?!

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:34.690
That's the plan!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:41.560
Kamille.

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:57.300
- Let's go, Kamille!
- <i>Lieutenant?!</i>

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:59.380
It's too dangerous to continue fighting here.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:04.950
Out of the way, Mouar!

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:11.220
Jerid.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:15.820
<i>We've landed in Von Braun City.</i>

00:19:16.100 --> 00:19:18.790
<i>Unless you stop attacking</i>
<i>and accept a ceasefire...</i>

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:21.840
<i>...we will completely destroy this city!</i>

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:23.300
<i>I repeat...!</i>

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.300
If we attacked with missiles
from this distance...

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.340
...we'd only be causing damage
to Von Braun City.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:29.340
They succeeded in tricking us.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.240
<i>Unless you stop attacking</i>
<i>and accept a ceasefire...!</i>

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.280
This is because we were slow in acting.

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:35.750
Hurry with arrangements
for reinforcements!

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:36.580
But how, sir?

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:38.350
You can travel along the surface
of the Moon!

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:40.720
Make people run to Granada
if they have to!

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:42.020
We need reinforcements!

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:44.410
Von Braun City has opened
its spaceport!

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:47.790
Order the mobile suit unit to retreat!

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:53.500
- Take this!
- <i>Fa!</i>

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:55.400
<i>Didn't you hear?! Retreat!</i>

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:57.440
Why? I can still fight!

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:04.470
Prolonging our fight will only
increase damage!

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.070
We'll wait for the next plan!

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.130
Wait, Jerid.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.800
Are you upset at me?

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.130
I haven't the time to be upset at you.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.930
Scirocco believes I'm skilled enough
to be used as a decoy.

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:35.570
That's why he used me, right?

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.410
I'm grateful for that.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:38.380
Jerid.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:40.640
This injury is nothing.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.210
Did Jerid say something?

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:44.050
No, sir!

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:44.910
Is that so.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:47.320
Lieutenant Commander Jamaican
is here to see you.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:50.950
Welcome, Lieutenant Commander
Jamaican.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:54.090
Don't get too comfortable, Scirocco.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.560
The Operation was a success.
I acknowledge that.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:01.930
But what if the A.E.U.G. had not retreated
as they did? What would you have done?

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.430
What do you have to say about that?!

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:07.330
Nothing, sir. You're absolutely right,
Lieutenant Commander.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:09.340
Perhaps I was being a little too reckless.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.070
I ask that from this point on,
you be in charge of this city's management.

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:15.340
It's too great of a task for me to handle.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.440
A-As long as you realize it.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:22.640
It's not easy acting out the role
I've been given.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:31.960
<i>Good job, Kamille.</i>

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:32.690
Thanks.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:36.760
- <i>I received that thing from you.</i>
- Huh? Oh, right! That's good.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:45.210
Fa?

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:48.110
You'd better rest
while you have the chance.

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:49.880
Our next plan is beginning shortly.

00:21:50.650 --> 00:21:51.980
Why won't you hit me?

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:54.750
I ignored orders to retreat.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.960
I don't care for kindness
if it's only to console!

00:21:58.030 --> 00:21:59.690
That's common until you get used to things.

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.230
- You did well out there.
- You're lying!

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:04.390
Lieutenant Emma!

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:07.160
I hope that outburst
is enough to calm you down, Fa.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.530
Astonaige was saying how impressed
he was...

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:11.570
...that you returned
without any major injury.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:14.400
Miss Reccoa.

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:19.770
She's excited from the intense battle.
Please look after her.

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:26.510
1969: Man set foot on the Moon
for the first time.

00:22:26.590 --> 00:22:30.180
Later, that piece of land became
the location of the central city on the Moon.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:36.690
And it was said that whoever controlled
Von Braun City controlled outer space.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:49.540
Kamille sneaks into Von Braun City.

00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:53.080
Due to his encounter
with Jerid and Mouar...

00:23:53.150 --> 00:23:56.550
...he's unable to return to the Argama
before it begins its counterattack.

00:23:57.520 --> 00:24:00.920
Can the A.E.U.G. recapture
Von Braun City?

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:06.550
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Counterattack".

00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:09.900
You will see the tears of time.

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Counterattack
